The comparison with old Gmail accounts also illustrates an important distinction. An established email account may contain years of communication and provide continuity, but its age does not constitute financial verification. Digital accounts can serve different purposes, and each type of account has its own requirements and significance.
The most useful lesson is therefore to focus on knowledge and responsible account management. Users can develop stronger digital-finance literacy by learning terminology, reading official documentation, maintaining accurate information, and organizing important correspondence.
These skills are increasingly relevant in modern life. Digital services are used for communication, employment, education, financial administration, subscriptions, and many other routine activities.
